---
// TERMS OF SERVICE — drafted August 2026. Deliberately short and specific to
// how BugBoss actually works: no contracts, quotes before work, guarantee
// defined on its own page (Rule 8).
//
// REVIEWED AND VERIFIED by the owner, August 2026. Re-check if the business
// changes how it quotes, guarantees, or takes payment — those three sections
// describe actual practice rather than boilerplate, so they go stale with the
// practice rather than with the calendar.
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Cta from '@/components/Cta.astro';
import { business, fullAddress } from '@/data/business';
import { webPageNode, breadcrumbNode } from '@/lib/schema';

const url = business.url + '/terms/';
const desc = `Terms for using the ${business.name} website and for the pest control and wildlife services we provide in Wisconsin.`;
const pageNodes = [
  webPageNode({ url, name: 'Terms of Service', description: desc }),
  breadcrumbNode(url, [{ name: 'Home', url: business.url + '/' }, { name: 'Terms of Service', url }]),
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description={desc} path="/terms/" pageNodes={pageNodes}>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated {business.contentReviewDateDisplay}.</p>

      <h2>Using this website</h2>
      <p>
        The information here — the Pest Library, the guides, the compliance pages — is provided
        to be genuinely useful, and we have taken care to get it right. It is general
        information about pests, wildlife and Wisconsin rules, not a substitute for an
        inspection of your property, and not legal advice. Conditions vary building to building,
        which is rather the point of having someone come and look.
      </p>

      <h2>Quotes and scheduling</h2>
      <p>
        We quote before we work. Quotes are based on what we can see at the time and on what you
        tell us; if the job turns out to be materially different once we are into it — a larger
        infestation, structural damage nobody knew about, access that is not what was described —
        we will tell you before doing extra work rather than after.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some work depends on conditions outside anyone's control. Bat exclusion in Wisconsin is
        legally timed around the maternity season and cannot simply be scheduled for a convenient
        week. Exterior treatments depend on weather. We will explain when that applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Access and preparation</h2>
      <p>
        Effective treatment usually needs access to the areas involved, and some jobs — bed bugs
        especially — need real preparation before we arrive. Where preparation is required we
        give you the list in advance and in writing. A treatment that fails because the property
        was not prepared or could not be accessed may need to be repeated at additional cost.
      </p>

      <h2>The guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        Our guarantee is defined in one place, with its covered pests and its exclusions written
        out: see <a href="/our-guarantee/">Our Guarantee</a>. Every use of the word
        “guaranteed” on this site refers to those terms and nothing broader. We do not offer a
        “lifetime” warranty and we explain why on that page.
      </p>

      <h2>No long-term contract</h2>
      <p>
        Quarterly service continues until you tell us to stop. There is no lock-in period and no
        cancellation fee — see <a href="/no-contracts/">No Contracts</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment is due as agreed when the work is quoted. Commercial accounts are invoiced {business.commercialTerms}.
      </p>

      <h2>Licensing and insurance</h2>
      <p>
        Work is performed by a licensed Wisconsin {business.owner.applicatorType} Pesticide
        Applicator, certification #{business.owner.licenseNumber}. The business carries general
        liability and workers' compensation insurance; a certificate is available on request. See
        <a href="/compliance/pesticide-applicator-licensing/">how to verify a Wisconsin applicator</a>
        if you would like to check independently, which we encourage.
      </p>

      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <p>
        Pest and wildlife work reduces and controls populations; no honest operator promises a
        permanent guarantee that nothing will ever return, because re-invasion from surrounding
        land is outside anyone's control. Our responsibility is limited to performing the agreed
        work competently and to honoring the guarantee on its stated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Wisconsin.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If these terms change we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {business.name}<br />
        {fullAddress}<br />
        <a href={`tel:${business.phoneTollFreeE164}`}>{business.phoneVanity}</a> · <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Cta />
</BaseLayout>
